icator.crossedOver(Number) - additional edge and type cases', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '-1000'}], 'expected': 'Rule instance of CrossedUpIndicatorRule; rule.isSatisfied(any index) == false (indicator values are always > -1000, so no crossing from <= to > can occur)', 'description': 'Constant far below the minimum series value. The underlying NumericIndicator never goes from <= -1000 to > -1000, therefore the rule must never be satisfied.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '3.5'}], 'expected': 'Rule instance of CrossedUpIndicatorRule; rule.isSatisfied(2) == true, rule.isSatisfied(1) == false', 'description': 'Series values: 3.5 at index\u202f0, 3.4 at index\u202f1, 3.6 at index\u202f2. The constant equals the first value; the rule should become satisfied only when the value crosses from ≤\u202f3.5 (index\u202f1) to >\u202f3.5 (index\u202f2).'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY'}], 'expected': 'Rule instance of CrossedUpIndicatorRule; rule.isSatisfied(any index) == false (a finite indicator can never cross above positive infinity)', 'description': 'Using Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY as the constant. No crossing can ever happen, so the rule must always be unsatisfied.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': 'Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY'}], 'expected': 'Rule instance of CrossedUpIndicatorRule; rule.isSatisfied(any index) == false (the indicator is always > -∞, thus never crosses from <= to >)', 'description': 'Using Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY as the constant. Since every numeric value is greater than -∞, there is no crossing event.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '2147483647'}], 'expected': 'Rule instance of CrossedUpIndicatorRule; rule.isSatisfied(any index) == false (series values stay well below Integer.MAX_VALUE)', 'description': 'Constant set to Integer.MAX_VALUE. The series values are far lower, so the rule never becomes satisfied.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'n', 'value': '0'}], 'expected': 'Rule i